{"schema":"metaphysica.path_patch/1","path":"chi_eff_route--constant_144","files":{"observer_report.json":{"base_sha256":"092f4db25c0ae272fd8c60eb9d37e9ed8bc05d5fb32bc1c00ef10052a0405b22","ops":[{"op":"replace","path":"/results/observer_independence/geometric_constants_nearly_invariant","value":true}]},"sections.json":{"base_sha256":"0875dba64a64e1cdfd037b13d85e25beee31abe2e949dd2357f5acdfc974a1bd","ops":[{"op":"replace","path":"/sections/0/contentBlocks/0/content","value":"<p>Principia Metaphysica is a speculative geometric model and has not been peer reviewed.</p><p><strong>Assumed.</strong> a 26D bulk of signature (24,2): 24 space directions and 2 times, one per shadow, split into two shadows. This is a postulate; nothing below derives it.</p><p><strong>Geometry.</strong> The internal space of each shadow is Y<sub>7</sub>, Joyce&rsquo;s resolution of T<sup>7</sup>/(&#8484;/2)<sup>3</sup>: a closed manifold with (b<sub>2</sub>, b<sub>3</sub>) = (12, 43) and n<sub>gen</sub> = b<sub>2</sub>/4 = 3, the number of singular involutions. A metric of holonomy exactly G<sub>2</sub> exists by Joyce 2000, Thm 11.6.1: 10 of 10 hypotheses are measured on the active seed and hold (closed by theorem). No explicit metric is claimed; none is known for any compact G<sub>2</sub> manifold.</p><p><strong>What follows.</strong> Read from the topology: the gauge content (CG.5), one K3 surface per singular involution (CG.9) and the effective index &chi;<sub>eff</sub> (an open ruling; the Euler characteristic of Y<sub>7</sub> is 0). Two results are negative: holonomy exactly G<sub>2</sub> excludes the confining sector that racetrack stabilisation needs (CG.10), and the leading flux potential cannot accelerate the universe (CG.11).</p><p><strong>Against data.</strong> Scoreboard: 27 pass, 15 marginal, 10 tension and 26 fail, with chi-squared 2.24e+09 over 67 scored rows. The model does not fit the data globally. Chirality, moduli stabilisation, dark energy and flavour are open.</p>"},{"op":"replace","path":"/sections/0/content_blocks/0/content","value":"<p>Principia Metaphysica is a speculative geometric model and has not been peer reviewed.</p><p><strong>Assumed.</strong> a 26D bulk of signature (24,2): 24 space directions and 2 times, one per shadow, split into two shadows. This is a postulate; nothing below derives it.</p><p><strong>Geometry.</strong> The internal space of each shadow is Y<sub>7</sub>, Joyce&rsquo;s resolution of T<sup>7</sup>/(&#8484;/2)<sup>3</sup>: a closed manifold with (b<sub>2</sub>, b<sub>3</sub>) = (12, 43) and n<sub>gen</sub> = b<sub>2</sub>/4 = 3, the number of singular involutions. A metric of holonomy exactly G<sub>2</sub> exists by Joyce 2000, Thm 11.6.1: 10 of 10 hypotheses are measured on the active seed and hold (closed by theorem). No explicit metric is claimed; none is known for any compact G<sub>2</sub> manifold.</p><p><strong>What follows.</strong> Read from the topology: the gauge content (CG.5), one K3 surface per singular involution (CG.9) and the effective index &chi;<sub>eff</sub> (an open ruling; the Euler characteristic of Y<sub>7</sub> is 0). Two results are negative: holonomy exactly G<sub>2</sub> excludes the confining sector that racetrack stabilisation needs (CG.10), and the leading flux potential cannot accelerate the universe (CG.11).</p><p><strong>Against data.</strong> Scoreboard: 27 pass, 15 marginal, 10 tension and 26 fail, with chi-squared 2.24e+09 over 67 scored rows. The model does not fit the data globally. Chirality, moduli stabilisation, dark energy and flavour are open.</p>"}]},"variants.json":{"base_sha256":"f52170689aeb8e192495b89efea4883be838a1738692f0913082c49b3de6910a","ops":[{"op":"replace","path":"/forks/spectral_index_route/source_read","value":"not_checked: path run overrides ['chi_eff_route']"},{"op":"replace","path":"/forks/h0_route/source_read","value":"not_checked: path run overrides ['chi_eff_route']"},{"op":"replace","path":"/forks/dark_energy_mechanism/source_read","valu